This project adapts code from the following open-source projects.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AudioCap — https://github.com/insidegui/AudioCap
Copyright (c) Guilherme Rambo. BSD 2-Clause License.

Adapted in: Sources/AudioRoutingEngine/CoreAudioProperties.swift
The AudioObjectID property-reading helpers (generic read / readString /
readArray over AudioObjectGetPropertyData, and the process-object list and
PID-translation accessors) follow AudioCap's ProcessTap/CoreAudioUtils.swift.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AudioRouter — https://github.com/RaidrDev/AudioRouter
Copyright (c) Raidr. MIT License.

Adapted in: Sources/AudioRoutingEngine/Route.swift
The shape of the aggregate-device creation dictionary (main sub-device + sub-tap
list + private flag) and the tap-then-aggregate-then-IOProc start/teardown
ordering follow AudioRouter's Sources/AudioRouter/ProcessRouter.swift. The
render block here is an independent implementation: it carries no class
reference (AudioRouter captures `[weak self]`), selects the tap buffer by
energy rather than by index, applies a smoothed gain ramp, and handles
non-interleaved output layouts.

